          "title": "Additional written application 2",
          "completeText": "Additional written application 2 This is optional written practice. It does not change required progress. Use the diagram or data with the question. Use the diagram or data with the question. In the first cross, a rabbit with the chinchilla coat colour is mated to a rabbit with a Himalayan coat colour that is known to be homozygous for this trait. Calculate the theoretical probability of this cross producing each of the following phenotypes shown below. Show the calculation or sequence and explain your reasoning. Use only the supplied evidence; do not invent observations. Optional response. Select Save response to collect it. Maximum 5000 characters. Save response",
